1
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:49,000
Live a good life out there.

2
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:49,880
Stay out of trouble.

3
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:51,680
Got it?

4
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:53,200
Yes.

5
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:55,080
Let's go.

6
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:58,160
Let's go.

7
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,120
Hua Lin

8
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:41,440
Hua Lin

9
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:44,800
You've grown taller.

10
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:53,240
How come you've lost weight?

11
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:03,840
Let me introduce you to Aunt Huilan.

12
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:08,520
Let's get going.

13
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:22,560
I'm leaving, Huilan.

14
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:26,200
I'll come visit you.

15
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:28,200
Get going.

16
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:09,640
Sister Lan.

17
00:04:09,640 --> 00:04:10,440
It's me.

18
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:43,600
Sister Lan

19
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,520
Hong Yu

20
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:03,440
What are you doing here?

21
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:04,880
How did you find me?

22
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:07,880
I said I'd come see you when I got out.

23
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:11,040
I'm here to see you.

24
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:27,200
What are you crying for?

25
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:29,480
We finally get to see each other.

26
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:30,360
Cheer up.

27
00:05:32,720 --> 00:05:33,280
Come on, let's go.

28
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:34,120
Hurry inside.

29
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:36,520
Come on in.

30
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:38,640
I haven't heard from you in ages.

31
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:40,360
Where have you been?

32
00:05:40,360 --> 00:05:41,760
How did you find me?

33
00:05:42,240 --> 00:05:44,640
I brought her up here, of course.

34
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:51,400
Are you still mad?

35
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:52,840
Stubborn as a mule.

36
00:05:58,720 --> 00:05:59,640
Yiran!

37
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:02,160
Yiran, come out here!

38
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:03,760
We have a guest!

39
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:05,320
Yiran, come on out!

40
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:09,600
Sister Lan.

41
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:11,400
When I was coming over,

42
00:06:12,120 --> 00:06:14,440
I didn't know what nice things to bring you.

43
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:17,080
These are flower pastries I made myself.

44
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:32,840
Yiran

45
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:33,960
Come on, let's go.

46
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:37,880
Let me introduce you to someone.

47
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:39,680
This is your Aunt Tang.

48
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:42,600
Your mom's best friend from inside.

49
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:45,080
You must be Yiran.

50
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:46,600
Hello, Aunt Tang.

51
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:49,200
Your mom talked about you all the time.

52
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:51,200
What a pretty girl.

53
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:52,280
Isn't she?

54
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:53,440
Thank you, Aunt Tang.

55
00:06:58,520 --> 00:06:59,720
Let's not just stand here.

56
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:01,600
Look.

57
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:04,480
Come on, take a look.

58
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:05,480
Sister Lan, look.

59
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:07,760
Yiran.

60
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:10,320
Auntie Juan made this plum wine herself.

61
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:11,800
It's your birthday, isn't it?

62
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:13,760
And Aunt Tang is here too.

63
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:15,960
We won't stop until we're drunk tonight.

64
00:07:15,960 --> 00:07:16,920
Come on, let's get some fruit.

65
00:07:16,920 --> 00:07:17,720
Quick, let's go.

66
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:18,880
Come on, over here.

67
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:24,000
Perfect timing.

68
00:07:24,640 --> 00:07:25,760
Have a seat.

69
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:36,520
Your hair has gone all white.

70
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:38,480
Why don't you dye it?

71
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:40,520
You know...

72
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:43,680
You should still dress yourself up a bit.

73
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:45,680
You can't just be so sloppy.

74
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:50,120
How have you been lately?

75
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:55,040
You just take it day by day.

76
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:57,000
Don't worry.

77
00:07:57,960 --> 00:07:59,160
I'm doing pretty well.

78
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:01,880
I mean, look at Aunt Tang.

79
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:03,680
She looks so honest.

80
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:05,600
I never thought she'd been inside too.

81
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:11,640
Still mad at your mom?

82
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:15,120
Auntie Juan.

83
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:17,720
Why do you always worry about everything?

84
00:08:18,840 --> 00:08:20,640
I'd rather not worry.

85
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:22,760
If only you two would give me a break.

86
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:26,320
You think your mom's years inside...

87
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:27,320
...were easy for her?

88
00:08:32,920 --> 00:08:33,440
Here.

89
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:36,840
Have some snacks to go with the wine.

90
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:43,480
Try some.

91
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:49,040
I really didn't expect...

92
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:52,120
...Sister Lan to do so many jobs
after getting out.

93
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:53,920
Whatever she tries, she ruins.

94
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:55,400
She's a total Industry jinx.

95
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,040
After all that...

96
00:08:57,040 --> 00:08:58,200
...she ended up doing a happy occasion.

97
00:08:58,520 --> 00:08:59,720
That's already pretty good.

98
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:01,560
When I got out...

99
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:03,440
...I just did odd jobs at a restaurant.

100
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:05,960
Washing bowls, doing dishes and stuff.

101
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:07,600
I don't know how to do anything else.

102
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:09,120
Nothing at all.

103
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:11,640
Hong Yu.

104
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:14,640
If Hua Lin ever gets married, come to me.

105
00:09:14,640 --> 00:09:16,640
I'll make sure it's perfect for him.

106
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:23,280
He's still young.

107
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:25,120
He's only in high school.

108
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:26,200
Let's wait till he grows up.

109
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:29,560
Yiran, come.

110
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:30,240
Try some.

111
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:32,880
Auntie Juan's homemade plum wine.

112
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:35,840
I... I think I'll pass.

113
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:37,040
I have to work tomorrow.

114
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:39,080
Enjoy yourselves, Aunties.

115
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:48,480
Did you two have a fight?

116
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:52,320
I wasn't fighting with her.

117
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:55,000
Just ignore her.

118
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:55,880
Come on, let's drink, drink up!

119
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:56,440
Come on.

120
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:08,160
Hong Yu.

121
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:10,760
What are your plans now?

122
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:14,720
I'm taking a train to my parents' home.

123
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:17,520
Right, right.

124
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:20,040
When we were inside, she told me

125
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:21,120
that her parents had passed away,

126
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:22,400
and she wanted to go back and visit.

127
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:25,440
Go back to visit their graves.

128
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:26,640
She misses them a lot.

129
00:10:28,040 --> 00:10:29,520
When do you plan to leave?

130
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:31,400
I'm planning to take tomorrow's train.

131
00:10:31,920 --> 00:10:32,920
So soon?

132
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,680
You just got here and you're leaving?

133
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:36,080
Stay and hang out for a couple more days.

134
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:37,640
I don't want to impose on you guys.

135
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:39,880
Look at her.

136
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:42,160
The two of us

137
00:10:42,520 --> 00:10:44,360
were in solitary confinement together.

138
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:45,800
For so many years,

139
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:47,440
we did absolutely everything together.

140
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:49,520
And now, she's being all polite with me.

141
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,360
I'm not just being polite.

142
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:53,720
Sister Lan will always be my Sister Lan.

143
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:01,080
Stop being so sentimental.

144
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:02,400
If you ask me,

145
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:03,360
come to my salon tomorrow.

146
00:11:03,360 --> 00:11:04,440
I'll do your hair for you.

147
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:06,680
So you can go back home looking pretty.

148
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:07,800
I couldn't impose like that.

149
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:09,520
There's nothing to feel bad about.

150
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:11,600
Let me tell you, Juanzi and I

151
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:14,320
have been old friends for decades.

152
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:16,160
But her skills are hit or miss.

153
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:17,520
You'll have to try your luck tomorrow.

154
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:19,960
If it's a miss, it's the machine's fault.

155
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:21,640
Come on.

156
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:22,600
Drink up, come on.

157
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:23,360
Let's have a drink.

158
00:11:24,520 --> 00:11:25,480
Are you staying or not?

159
00:11:26,040 --> 00:11:26,640
Alright.

160
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:28,600
I'll stay a couple more days.

161
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:30,720
Great, come on.

162
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:36,400
It's settled then, you're staying.

163
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:37,600
Okay.

164
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:42,160
Bottoms up.

165
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:44,000
Okay.

166
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:51,120
You can really drink!

167
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:56,480
You...

168
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:58,720
You should just

169
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:00,400
go and apologize to her.

170
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:04,320
Didn't I apologize earlier during dinner?

171
00:12:04,320 --> 00:12:06,280
I've apologized enough already.

172
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:08,040
Does she want me to get on my knees?

173
00:12:08,040 --> 00:12:09,920
Just saying it verbally doesn't count.

174
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:12,120
Did you forget what you did

175
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:13,320
when we were having BBQ

176
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:14,400
last time?

177
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:17,920
I'm not writing another promise letter.

178
00:12:18,560 --> 00:12:21,280
I'm already pathetic enough as a mother.

179
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:24,160
What mother isn't pathetic?

180
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:26,240
Who has it easy?

181
00:12:28,160 --> 00:12:30,280
Aren't I pretty pathetic too?

182
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:34,000
The moon is so round today.

183
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:36,880
Because today,

184
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:41,040
my two best sisters are right beside me.

185
00:12:46,760 --> 00:12:48,960
The outside world really is better.

186
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:53,400
How about this?

187
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:56,720
Us three pathetic moms should go on a trip.

188
00:12:56,720 --> 00:12:58,400
Let's go see the outside world together.

189
00:12:58,400 --> 00:12:59,200
What do you say?

190
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:00,960
Agreed.

191
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:05,640
Are you in?

192
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:07,480
I'm in.

193
00:13:08,920 --> 00:13:11,000
Why is she always a beat behind?

194
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,160
She really is a beat behind.

195
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:23,960
You ask me how deep my love is...

196
00:13:24,880 --> 00:13:26,680
I love you!

197
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:36,520
I'm so happy!

198
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:37,440
Juanzi.

199
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:03,280
Do you think your mom spent all these years

200
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:04,440
living comfortably in there?

201
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:10,120
How she's been doing in there

202
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:11,600
has nothing to do with me.

203
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:13,400
I'm the one who feels wronged.

204
00:14:20,920 --> 00:14:21,960
I'll head over first then.

205
00:14:21,960 --> 00:14:22,800
Go ahead.

206
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:30,160
Are you okay?

207
00:14:31,480 --> 00:14:32,280
I'm perfectly fine.

208
00:14:34,520 --> 00:14:36,960
Are you still mad about yesterday?

209
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:38,640
Why would I be mad at you?

210
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:43,000
I told you they wouldn't work out.

211
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,280
Enemies are bound to cross paths.

212
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:45,440
You know nothing.

213
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:46,800
The best show is yet to come.

214
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:51,000
Morning.

215
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:52,320
Hurry up and go to work.

216
00:14:56,280 --> 00:14:57,400
Anger is bad for your health.

217
00:15:00,160 --> 00:15:01,120
Ignore him.

218
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:02,120
Here.

219
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:05,160
Your brother...

220
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:07,840
where did he go dressed like that?

221
00:15:08,520 --> 00:15:12,040
Him? He went on a blind date.

222
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:16,480
A blind date?

223
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:18,600
Going on a blind date is good.

224
00:15:19,680 --> 00:15:21,040
He's not getting any younger.

225
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:22,600
I'm just kidding.

226
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:25,200
As a reform pioneer, Xiaoxitian was invited

227
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:28,000
to the city's funeral reform conference.

228
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:28,920
My brother went to give a speech.

229
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:34,240
How are things with Aunt Huilan?

230
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:36,080
Everyone keeps telling me

231
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:37,280
that Wu Huilan is doing it for my good.

232
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:39,160
She's doing it for my good,

233
00:15:39,160 --> 00:15:40,480
but who can I talk to about my pain?

234
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:42,280
If I speak too mildly to her,

235
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:43,040
she won't listen.

236
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:44,120
She just won't take it in.

237
00:15:44,120 --> 00:15:44,680
If I speak too harshly,

238
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:46,560
it makes me look unfilial.

239
00:15:46,560 --> 00:15:47,600
Let me tell you, she...

240
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:49,400
I don't want to hear this today.

241
00:15:49,400 --> 00:15:50,560
Let's not talk about this, okay?

242
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:56,160
This color looks great.

243
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:58,680
Your lips are actually quite sexy.

244
00:15:59,640 --> 00:16:00,640
Don't laugh.

245
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:02,120
I'm telling the truth.

246
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:04,040
Pucker your lips a bit.

247
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:05,160
Like this.

248
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:06,320
Yes.

249
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:09,760
Perfect.

250
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:11,200
So beautiful.

251
00:16:11,200 --> 00:16:11,840
Really.

252
00:16:11,840 --> 00:16:12,240
Looks great.

253
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:13,480
Your complexion instantly looks better.

254
00:16:13,760 --> 00:16:15,520
Come pick a hairclip, quick.

255
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:17,280
I feel like something's missing on your head.

256
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:23,440
You have such great taste.

257
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:26,240
When I was young, I loved wearing
these little red flowers.

258
00:16:26,240 --> 00:16:26,720
Here.

259
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:34,520
So pretty.

260
00:16:35,480 --> 00:16:37,600
Come, let's go look in the big mirror.

261
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:38,840
Come on.

262
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:44,120
See for yourself.

263
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:46,800
Clothes make the person.

264
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:48,480
You look completely different now.

265
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:52,040
Yiran is back.

266
00:16:57,480 --> 00:16:58,240
Yiran.

267
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:00,560
Your mom has dinner ready.

268
00:17:00,560 --> 00:17:01,960
She's waiting for you to eat.

269
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:07,840
You look great, Aunt Tang.

270
00:17:07,840 --> 00:17:09,240
This look really suits you.

271
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:10,720
I told you, your Aunt Tang

272
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:13,200
already has such a pretty face.

273
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:14,600
With this on, it's like

274
00:17:14,600 --> 00:17:16,040
adding a peony to a phoenix's crown.

275
00:17:16,040 --> 00:17:17,200
Prettier than ever.

276
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:19,000
Let's go eat.

277
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,040
Time to eat.

278
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:20,760
Let's go eat.

279
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:28,200
Call her again.

280
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:29,280
Call her once more.

281
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:31,360
Yiran.

282
00:17:32,280 --> 00:17:34,080
Uncle Daren said tomorrow

283
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:35,560
he's taking us to Mangjian Village.

284
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:36,240
Are you going?

285
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:37,480
No, I have to work.

286
00:17:37,760 --> 00:17:39,560
Then come over and eat!

287
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:41,560
I already ate at the banquet.

288
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:52,320
Oh my god.

289
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:54,400
Why are you covering it up?

290
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:56,240
Wang Daren, Wang Daren.

291
00:17:56,240 --> 00:17:57,800
Wang Daren, does it look good?

292
00:17:58,840 --> 00:18:00,120
It's so glamorous.

293
00:18:02,720 --> 00:18:03,720
Why did you put that on?

294
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:04,800
That red lipstick

295
00:18:04,800 --> 00:18:06,800
looks like you drank chicken blood.

296
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:08,560
What kind of day is this?

297
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:10,600
Come on, come on.

298
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:14,680
You only opened the door for her,
but not for me. Seriously.

299
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:16,800
You get jealous over everything. Honestly.

300
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:18,000
Get in, get in.

301
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:30,560
Juanzi, you left Yangyang at home alone.

302
00:18:30,560 --> 00:18:31,760
Aren't you worried?

303
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:34,120
What's there to be worried about?

304
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:36,680
Yangyang has someone looking after him.

305
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:39,800
Our Juanzi is feeling the breeze
of youth right now.

306
00:18:42,280 --> 00:18:44,320
Having a fit? Who's having a fit?

307
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:46,920
You've never felt that breeze anyway.

308
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:54,560
What's wrong? Got a toothache?

309
00:18:58,280 --> 00:18:59,840
What are you doing, Wang Daren?

310
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:01,360
You look like a roly-poly riding a rabbit.

311
00:19:01,360 --> 00:19:02,520
Seriously, you scared me to death.

312
00:19:02,520 --> 00:19:03,640
My stomach's acting up.

313
00:19:03,640 --> 00:19:04,360
I can't hold it.

314
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:05,520
Okay, just don't poop in the car.

315
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:06,320
Wait for me a sec.

316
00:19:12,920 --> 00:19:14,960
Uncle Daren, what's wrong?

317
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:17,400
Where... where is your restroom?

318
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:19,920
Okay.

319
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:27,000
Sister Lan.

320
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,440
Isn't this Yiran's workplace?

321
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:29,800
Aren't you going down to see her?

322
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:31,000
Why would I go down there?

323
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:32,240
Just to ask for trouble?

324
00:19:35,680 --> 00:19:36,920
Xiaoxitian.

325
00:19:38,600 --> 00:19:40,320
Yiran works in the funeral business.

326
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:43,720
Young people today are really brave.

327
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:45,480
The two of us, mother and daughter.

328
00:19:46,040 --> 00:19:48,080
One in happy occasions, one in funerals.

329
00:19:48,080 --> 00:19:49,760
Weddings and funerals clash.

330
00:19:49,760 --> 00:19:52,240
We're destined to be mortal enemies.

331
00:19:52,360 --> 00:19:53,320
Slow down, slow down, slow down.

332
00:19:53,320 --> 00:19:54,000
Uncle Daren.

333
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:55,920
Have some hot water first.

334
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:56,960
It hurts so much.

335
00:19:59,080 --> 00:20:00,320
Take it easy, take it easy.

336
00:20:03,080 --> 00:20:04,480
Let me go get you some medicine.

337
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:05,720
No need, no need.

338
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:07,400
I just ate something bad.

339
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:10,240
Yiran.

340
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:12,480
Can you do me a favor?

341
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:14,160
Drive your mom and her friends?

342
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:17,600
Uncle Daren, I...

343
00:20:20,320 --> 00:20:22,800
I really ate something bad.

344
00:20:22,800 --> 00:20:26,040
And I don't want to ruin the fun
for your mom and her friends.

345
00:20:27,760 --> 00:20:28,560
Yiran.

346
00:20:29,120 --> 00:20:32,200
Just consider it doing your Uncle Daren a favor.

347
00:20:35,080 --> 00:20:36,080
I can't hold it, I can't.

348
00:20:36,080 --> 00:20:36,720
I can't hold it in anymore.

349
00:20:36,720 --> 00:20:37,800
Please, Yiran.

350
00:20:37,800 --> 00:20:38,560
I'm begging you.

351
00:20:38,840 --> 00:20:39,640
Please.

352
00:20:45,280 --> 00:20:46,080
Okay.

353
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:47,600
Let me confirm the address with you.

354
00:20:48,360 --> 00:20:49,840
Number 36, Mangjian Village, right?

355
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:51,800
Okay, okay, I'll be right there.

356
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:52,760
Bye.

357
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:55,960
What are you standing here for?

358
00:20:56,320 --> 00:20:57,520
You're going to Mangjian too?

359
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:01,160
Come with me.

360
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:05,480
Uncle Daren.

361
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:07,040
I... I'm leaving.

362
00:21:33,640 --> 00:21:35,200
Ming, oh, Ming.

363
00:21:36,120 --> 00:21:38,840
Your daughter and wife are too tough to deal with.

364
00:21:39,680 --> 00:21:41,360
This is as much as I can help.

365
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:44,880
The rest is up to their own fate.

366
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:53,440
Summer, summer quietly slipped away

367
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:55,360
Leaving behind little secrets

368
00:21:56,040 --> 00:21:57,240
How does the next line go?

369
00:21:57,520 --> 00:21:59,200
Buried in the heart, buried...

370
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:09,000
Take a good look.

371
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:10,160
Isn't Xiao Chen handsome?

372
00:22:11,640 --> 00:22:12,600
He is pretty handsome.

373
00:22:13,080 --> 00:22:14,120
Of course he is.

374
00:22:14,280 --> 00:22:16,640
How could Lecang's Andy Lau
not be handsome?

375
00:22:19,280 --> 00:22:21,200
Are they...

376
00:22:21,960 --> 00:22:23,520
You've got a sharp eye.

377
00:22:23,520 --> 00:22:25,360
Don't go playing matchmaker.

378
00:22:25,360 --> 00:22:27,440
Those two are just colleagues.

379
00:22:27,440 --> 00:22:28,120
Speaking so loudly.

380
00:22:28,120 --> 00:22:29,480
It's so awkward for them.

381
00:22:29,480 --> 00:22:30,320
You're asking for it!

382
00:22:30,320 --> 00:22:32,760
Talking so loud. Afraid they won't hear?

383
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:34,160
Hong Yu.

384
00:22:34,160 --> 00:22:35,760
Have an orange. It's sweet and sour.

385
00:22:35,760 --> 00:22:37,080
Just like that feeling.

386
00:22:37,080 --> 00:22:38,680
Wu Huilan, can you be a little quieter?

387
00:22:38,680 --> 00:22:40,040
Just sit still in the car.

388
00:22:40,760 --> 00:22:41,560
And also,

389
00:22:42,280 --> 00:22:44,320
we're just ordinary colleagues.

390
00:22:44,720 --> 00:22:45,440
Right?

391
00:22:48,040 --> 00:22:49,920
"Right?" She's asking you, "Right?"

392
00:22:49,920 --> 00:22:50,960
Auntie, you know how it is.

393
00:22:50,960 --> 00:22:53,120
The two of us just grew up together.

394
00:22:53,120 --> 00:22:54,080
Innocent childhood friends.

395
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:55,400
Childhood sweethearts.

396
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:56,000
A perfect match.

397
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:58,840
See? Your Aunt Hong Yu can see it too.

398
00:23:02,240 --> 00:23:03,240
Xiao Chen.

399
00:23:03,240 --> 00:23:04,920
Weren't you going to feed her that orange?

400
00:23:05,160 --> 00:23:06,480
You know what to do.

401
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:08,480
Auntie, Auntie.

402
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:09,600
I'll say it one more time.

403
00:23:25,840 --> 00:23:26,920
Still staring at your phone?

404
00:23:27,200 --> 00:23:28,400
You got a death wish?

405
00:23:43,680 --> 00:23:44,600
What's going on?

406
00:23:45,080 --> 00:23:46,760
Learn some manners! How do you even drive?

407
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:53,760
Get out.

408
00:23:54,840 --> 00:23:55,640
Get out of the car!

409
00:23:55,880 --> 00:23:56,760
Get out!

410
00:23:56,760 --> 00:23:57,520
What do you want?

411
00:23:57,520 --> 00:23:58,440
You got a problem with me?

412
00:23:59,480 --> 00:24:00,360
Do you even know how to drive?

413
00:24:00,360 --> 00:24:01,120
Why the hell are you honking?

414
00:24:01,120 --> 00:24:01,920
Do I know how to drive?

415
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:02,800
Keep your eyes on the road.

416
00:24:02,800 --> 00:24:03,840
Why were you on your phone?

417
00:24:03,840 --> 00:24:04,640
Me on my phone?

418
00:24:04,640 --> 00:24:05,880
None of your damn business if I'm on my phone!

419
00:24:05,880 --> 00:24:06,360
None of my business?

420
00:24:06,360 --> 00:24:08,080
Bro, you swerved while on your phone.

421
00:24:08,080 --> 00:24:09,680
Texting and driving, and cutting me off!

422
00:24:09,680 --> 00:24:10,280
What's wrong with you?

423
00:24:10,280 --> 00:24:10,760
Let me handle this.

424
00:24:10,760 --> 00:24:12,480
The dashcam caught everything.

425
00:24:12,480 --> 00:24:13,520
So what? So what if it did?

426
00:24:13,960 --> 00:24:14,960
Get over here.

427
00:24:15,360 --> 00:24:16,800
I need a word with you.

428
00:24:30,560 --> 00:24:31,560
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

429
00:24:31,560 --> 00:24:32,280
My bad.

430
00:24:32,280 --> 00:24:32,880
Get lost.

431
00:24:32,880 --> 00:24:33,560
I'll get going.

432
00:24:33,560 --> 00:24:34,320
Sorry, ma'am.

433
00:24:34,320 --> 00:24:34,680
I'm sorry.

434
00:24:42,440 --> 00:24:43,760
It's no big deal.

435
00:24:43,760 --> 00:24:44,880
It's settled now, right?

436
00:24:44,880 --> 00:24:45,600
Get in.

437
00:24:46,480 --> 00:24:47,120
Let's go.

438
00:24:47,880 --> 00:24:48,760
What did you say?

439
00:24:48,760 --> 00:24:49,880
It's no big deal.

440
00:24:50,240 --> 00:24:51,080
It's all a misunderstanding.

441
00:24:51,080 --> 00:24:51,720
Let's go.

442
00:24:52,760 --> 00:24:53,880
Not bad.

443
00:25:30,680 --> 00:25:31,520
Zhang Lijuan

444
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:33,760
Can you come over and help with the bags?

445
00:25:33,760 --> 00:25:35,160
Am I your servant?

446
00:25:35,600 --> 00:25:37,440
Sister Lan, don't be in such a rush.

447
00:25:37,440 --> 00:25:38,800
We're out having fun. Just take it slow.

448
00:25:38,800 --> 00:25:40,320
Look at how beautiful the scenery is.

449
00:25:40,720 --> 00:25:42,240
Give all the heavy stuff to me.

450
00:25:42,240 --> 00:25:43,800
I'll carry these heavy bags.

451
00:25:44,320 --> 00:25:45,640
Xiao Chen is so attentive.

452
00:25:45,640 --> 00:25:46,480
Seriously.

453
00:25:46,480 --> 00:25:47,680
You're so considerate.

454
00:25:47,680 --> 00:25:49,520
Unlike some people, just staring
like a lost puppy.

455
00:25:49,520 --> 00:25:50,520
Not helping at all.

456
00:25:52,840 --> 00:25:54,080
Aunt Tang, here, let me take that.

457
00:25:54,080 --> 00:25:54,600
No need.

458
00:25:54,600 --> 00:25:55,440
It's fine.

459
00:25:55,960 --> 00:25:56,920
Auntie Juan, let me take that.

460
00:25:56,920 --> 00:25:59,120
See? Isn't Yiran being helpful too?

461
00:26:01,240 --> 00:26:01,920
Take it.

462
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:04,400
I got it.

463
00:26:05,280 --> 00:26:06,120
Hold this.

464
00:26:10,080 --> 00:26:11,360
Why won't you let me carry it?

465
00:26:12,040 --> 00:26:13,240
Are you unhappy with me?

466
00:26:13,240 --> 00:26:14,120
Then I'll leave.

467
00:26:14,120 --> 00:26:15,520
Are you trying to pick a fight with me?

468
00:26:15,520 --> 00:26:17,320
I say one word and you reply with ten,
don't you?

469
00:26:17,320 --> 00:26:18,880
Say one less word, and I'll spare you ten.

470
00:26:18,880 --> 00:26:19,560
No, you...

471
00:26:19,560 --> 00:26:20,480
Alright, alright.

472
00:26:20,480 --> 00:26:22,080
Just drop it.

473
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:23,920
Don't ruin the mood for our trip.

474
00:26:25,480 --> 00:26:27,720
This tree must be over a thousand years old.

475
00:26:30,680 --> 00:26:31,360
Look.

476
00:26:31,800 --> 00:26:33,080
Isn't it pretty?

477
00:26:36,280 --> 00:26:37,080
Mister.

478
00:26:37,080 --> 00:26:38,920
Buy a bouquet for your girlfriend.

479
00:26:41,240 --> 00:26:42,680
I'm not his girlfriend.

480
00:26:42,680 --> 00:26:44,080
Go ask someone else, little girl.

481
00:26:45,680 --> 00:26:46,480
Wait a minute.

482
00:26:47,320 --> 00:26:48,360
How much for a bouquet?

483
00:26:48,360 --> 00:26:49,720
Ten yuan.

484
00:26:49,720 --> 00:26:52,440
Give it to the lady, she'll definitely love it.

485
00:26:52,560 --> 00:26:53,800
Alright, I'll take them all.

486
00:26:54,360 --> 00:26:55,160
Thank you.

487
00:27:00,520 --> 00:27:01,840
Transferred.

488
00:27:05,240 --> 00:27:06,080
Thank you, little girl.

489
00:27:06,080 --> 00:27:06,800
Thank you, mister.

490
00:27:06,800 --> 00:27:07,560
Bye.

491
00:27:07,560 --> 00:27:08,360
Bye.

492
00:27:10,760 --> 00:27:12,000
Smells nice.

493
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:14,320
Three beautiful ladies.

494
00:27:14,840 --> 00:27:15,280
Here.

495
00:27:15,280 --> 00:27:16,440
A bouquet for you.

496
00:27:16,440 --> 00:27:17,840
For us?

497
00:27:17,840 --> 00:27:18,680
You want this one?

498
00:27:18,680 --> 00:27:19,120
Alright then.

499
00:27:19,120 --> 00:27:19,720
Thank you.

500
00:27:19,720 --> 00:27:20,640
The pink one is for you.

501
00:27:21,560 --> 00:27:22,800
You can hold it for photos.

502
00:27:24,600 --> 00:27:25,400
You guys keep looking around.

503
00:27:25,400 --> 00:27:26,520
You really are so considerate.

504
00:27:31,560 --> 00:27:32,440
Yiran.

505
00:27:32,440 --> 00:27:33,840
I'll go drop something off for the client.

506
00:27:34,560 --> 00:27:35,640
The guesthouse is right over there.

507
00:27:35,640 --> 00:27:36,880
Call me if you need anything.

508
00:27:36,880 --> 00:27:37,840
I'll just be in the village.

509
00:27:38,600 --> 00:27:39,800
Take good care of these three
beautiful ladies.

510
00:27:40,320 --> 00:27:41,480
You talk too much.

511
00:27:41,480 --> 00:27:42,320
Just get going.

512
00:27:44,640 --> 00:27:45,360
I'll head over now then.

513
00:27:45,360 --> 00:27:45,880
See you later.

514
00:27:45,880 --> 00:27:47,200
Hurry back.

515
00:27:54,840 --> 00:27:56,120
Here.

516
00:27:56,120 --> 00:27:56,920
Yiran, here.

517
00:28:11,400 --> 00:28:12,480
Hong Yu.

518
00:28:12,800 --> 00:28:15,200
What exactly did you say to that driver?

519
00:28:18,080 --> 00:28:19,240
If I tell you...

520
00:28:20,040 --> 00:28:21,360
...it's a bit embarrassing.

521
00:28:21,360 --> 00:28:22,440
We're all family here.

522
00:28:22,440 --> 00:28:24,480
Who cares if it's embarrassing? Tell us.

523
00:28:24,480 --> 00:28:25,000
Here.

524
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:25,840
Thanks, Auntie Juan.

525
00:28:47,120 --> 00:28:48,400
What is it, old lady? Looking for trouble?

526
00:28:51,480 --> 00:28:52,360
Take a good look.

527
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:55,800
Do you know why I killed someone?

528
00:28:57,840 --> 00:28:59,680
Because some blind fool

529
00:28:59,680 --> 00:29:00,800
bullied a woman.

530
00:29:01,680 --> 00:29:02,200
Ma'am...

531
00:29:02,200 --> 00:29:02,920
Um, I...

532
00:29:03,640 --> 00:29:04,840
I... I'll be going now.

533
00:29:04,840 --> 00:29:05,720
Sorry, ma'am.

534
00:29:05,720 --> 00:29:06,440
I'm sorry.

535
00:29:08,240 --> 00:29:09,880
Right after I got out of prison,

536
00:29:10,040 --> 00:29:11,560
someone tried to rob me.

537
00:29:12,160 --> 00:29:13,280
I don't know why,

538
00:29:13,280 --> 00:29:14,440
but when they saw this piece of paper,

539
00:29:14,440 --> 00:29:15,480
they turned and ran.

540
00:29:15,480 --> 00:29:17,080
They even gave my stuff back.

541
00:29:17,080 --> 00:29:18,080
So I was thinking,

542
00:29:18,080 --> 00:29:19,480
having been to prison

543
00:29:20,120 --> 00:29:22,000
isn't completely useless.

544
00:29:23,200 --> 00:29:24,760
At least people are scared of you.

545
00:29:27,920 --> 00:29:28,960
So you just

546
00:29:29,560 --> 00:29:31,200
carry it with you all the time.

547
00:29:33,080 --> 00:29:34,600
Just throw this thing away.

548
00:29:36,440 --> 00:29:38,640
So many bad memories...

549
00:29:38,640 --> 00:29:40,880
Seeing it every day gives you a headache.

550
00:29:45,240 --> 00:29:46,000
Hong Yu.

551
00:29:46,000 --> 00:29:47,560
Tell us about what happened inside.

552
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:49,120
What's there to tell about being inside?

553
00:29:49,120 --> 00:29:49,840
Drink, drink, let's drink.

554
00:29:49,840 --> 00:29:50,560
Come on, come on.

555
00:29:50,920 --> 00:29:52,000
You guys have no idea.

556
00:29:52,280 --> 00:29:54,080
When Sister Lan was inside,

557
00:29:54,080 --> 00:29:55,560
she was the big boss.

558
00:29:57,200 --> 00:29:58,280
The big boss?

559
00:29:59,520 --> 00:30:00,920
A big boss who just caused trouble.

560
00:30:01,320 --> 00:30:02,120
Really.

561
00:30:02,120 --> 00:30:02,760
Back then,

562
00:30:02,760 --> 00:30:04,520
there was a bully in our cell.

563
00:30:04,520 --> 00:30:06,240
She bullied me every day.

564
00:30:06,240 --> 00:30:07,880
Sister Lan couldn't stand it.

565
00:30:07,880 --> 00:30:08,960
One time in the cafeteria,

566
00:30:08,960 --> 00:30:10,200
she was bullying me again.

567
00:30:10,200 --> 00:30:11,720
Sister Lan grabbed a spoon

568
00:30:11,720 --> 00:30:14,040
and whacked her a few times.

569
00:30:14,040 --> 00:30:16,080
The spoon was bent out of shape.

570
00:30:16,080 --> 00:30:18,840
And a huge lump instantly grew on her head.

571
00:30:18,840 --> 00:30:20,200
From then on,

572
00:30:20,680 --> 00:30:22,640
whenever that bully saw Sister Lan,

573
00:30:22,640 --> 00:30:23,880
she'd turn and run.

574
00:30:23,880 --> 00:30:24,880
It was so satisfying.

575
00:30:25,960 --> 00:30:26,520
Enough.

576
00:30:26,520 --> 00:30:27,520
Don't talk about that.

577
00:30:27,520 --> 00:30:28,880
I even got thrown in solitary for it.

578
00:30:29,480 --> 00:30:31,240
You're a troublemaker wherever you go.

579
00:30:33,080 --> 00:30:34,080
Li Yiran.

580
00:30:35,280 --> 00:30:36,920
Don't go on and on about it.

581
00:30:40,040 --> 00:30:42,560
We're family. No grudges overnight, right?

582
00:30:42,560 --> 00:30:43,400
Right?

583
00:30:44,360 --> 00:30:45,080
Let's drink, drink.

584
00:30:45,080 --> 00:30:45,600
Drink.

585
00:30:53,080 --> 00:30:54,040
Yiran,

586
00:30:54,640 --> 00:30:56,160
back then, your mom...

587
00:30:56,160 --> 00:30:57,440
really took care of me.

588
00:30:58,240 --> 00:30:59,720
She took care of you on the inside.

589
00:30:59,720 --> 00:31:01,200
She had your backs.

590
00:31:02,240 --> 00:31:04,840
Do you know how I survived on the outside?

591
00:31:07,480 --> 00:31:08,920
Let me think back.

592
00:31:09,600 --> 00:31:11,160
In those years,

593
00:31:11,160 --> 00:31:14,760
people stuck notes saying
"murderer's daughter"

594
00:31:14,760 --> 00:31:16,560
on my back.

595
00:31:16,560 --> 00:31:18,200
Carved words into my desk.

596
00:31:18,200 --> 00:31:20,160
Put fake blood in my backpack.

597
00:31:20,160 --> 00:31:21,200
Pinned me to the ground

598
00:31:21,200 --> 00:31:22,920
and poured soda over my head.

599
00:31:22,920 --> 00:31:25,080
Called me an unwanted wild child.

600
00:31:28,600 --> 00:31:30,120
Sometimes the neighbors took pity on me

601
00:31:30,880 --> 00:31:32,600
and brought me to their house for dinner.

602
00:31:32,600 --> 00:31:33,440
I didn't even...

603
00:31:33,440 --> 00:31:34,720
I didn't even dare to take an extra bite.

604
00:31:34,720 --> 00:31:36,800
I was afraid they'd get sick of me.

605
00:31:38,520 --> 00:31:39,840
When I went to college,

606
00:31:39,840 --> 00:31:41,640
I had to work multiple part-time jobs.

607
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:42,800
I wouldn't eat breakfast.

608
00:31:42,800 --> 00:31:43,640
I'd just power through.

609
00:31:44,480 --> 00:31:45,600
I'd buy one meal at noon,

610
00:31:46,200 --> 00:31:47,560
and eat the leftovers for dinner.

611
00:31:50,760 --> 00:31:52,360
It completely cured my picky eating habit.

612
00:32:00,880 --> 00:32:01,840
Wu Huilan.

613
00:32:02,440 --> 00:32:04,840
You only ever care about your own feelings.

614
00:32:05,120 --> 00:32:08,000
You always force what you want onto me,

615
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:10,200
but you never put yourself in my shoes.

616
00:32:15,120 --> 00:32:17,200
Do you have any idea? The house...

617
00:32:17,200 --> 00:32:19,480
The house is the only thing Dad left me.

618
00:32:21,480 --> 00:32:22,280
Six years.

619
00:32:26,840 --> 00:32:28,520
I struggled in Shanghai for six years.

620
00:32:30,560 --> 00:32:32,280
I felt that only this house was our home.

621
00:32:32,280 --> 00:32:34,000
A home for our family of three.

622
00:32:35,360 --> 00:32:36,920
How could you sell this home?

623
00:32:36,920 --> 00:32:38,280
Do you even have a heart?

624
00:32:42,760 --> 00:32:43,880
That house was our real home.

625
00:32:43,880 --> 00:32:45,640
Not your so-called new house.

626
00:33:11,600 --> 00:33:12,680
Are you done?

627
00:33:17,480 --> 00:33:18,400
The two of us...

628
00:33:19,800 --> 00:33:21,240
...are just a doomed pair.

629
00:33:22,280 --> 00:33:23,520
In 1999,

630
00:33:24,240 --> 00:33:25,720
on October 28th,

631
00:33:25,720 --> 00:33:27,360
at 1:19 AM,

632
00:33:27,880 --> 00:33:28,920
you were born.

633
00:33:29,600 --> 00:33:30,800
You were in there,

634
00:33:30,800 --> 00:33:32,640
torturing me for a whole day and night.

635
00:33:32,640 --> 00:33:34,320
Just sitting in there, refusing to come out.

636
00:33:35,280 --> 00:33:37,720
Finally, the doctor had to cut me open

637
00:33:37,720 --> 00:33:39,040
to take you out.

638
00:33:39,920 --> 00:33:42,560
As soon as you were born,
you had a fever every day.

639
00:33:42,560 --> 00:33:44,800
I carried you to the hospital
every single day,

640
00:33:44,800 --> 00:33:46,440
back and forth.

641
00:33:46,440 --> 00:33:48,800
I was so worried my hair fell out in clumps.

642
00:33:51,320 --> 00:33:52,280
When you were six,

643
00:33:53,120 --> 00:33:54,680
you loved wearing that green sweater.

644
00:33:54,920 --> 00:33:57,280
You wore that green sweater all year round.

645
00:33:57,760 --> 00:33:59,240
You wouldn't even take it off in summer.

646
00:33:59,240 --> 00:34:00,680
You got heat rash all over.

647
00:34:00,680 --> 00:34:01,880
I was worried sick again.

648
00:34:01,880 --> 00:34:03,040
Running to the hospital every day.

649
00:34:05,160 --> 00:34:06,800
You had a hard time out there
for eight years,

650
00:34:06,800 --> 00:34:07,800
I know that.

651
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:10,760
You hate me, I know that too.

652
00:34:12,240 --> 00:34:14,640
Do you think my eight years in there
were easy?

653
00:34:18,600 --> 00:34:19,600
If it weren't for you,

654
00:34:19,600 --> 00:34:23,440
I'd have died countless times by now.

655
00:34:25,320 --> 00:34:26,600
It was just because of you

656
00:34:27,280 --> 00:34:29,240
that I held onto my last breath to get out.

657
00:34:31,400 --> 00:34:32,800
After I got out,

658
00:34:33,480 --> 00:34:34,760
I told myself,

659
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:37,560
I want to start over with my daughter.

660
00:34:40,480 --> 00:34:43,320
I want to give her a new home,

661
00:34:43,320 --> 00:34:45,880
and not let her live in that awful past,

662
00:34:45,880 --> 00:34:48,480
thinking about those bad things every day.

663
00:34:50,560 --> 00:34:51,920
A person's life

664
00:34:52,120 --> 00:34:53,760
isn't too long,

665
00:34:53,760 --> 00:34:55,160
but it isn't too short either.

666
00:34:55,320 --> 00:34:57,080
You have to make yourself happy!

667
00:34:59,280 --> 00:35:01,960
You think about unhappy things
every single day.

668
00:35:02,800 --> 00:35:04,880
When are you ever going to move on?

669
00:35:06,960 --> 00:35:09,040
I don't even know what the hell I did wrong!

670
00:35:12,080 --> 00:35:13,080
You're not wrong.

671
00:35:13,080 --> 00:35:13,880
How could you ever be wrong?

672
00:35:13,880 --> 00:35:15,280
You're always right.

673
00:35:15,280 --> 00:35:17,560
You're always so full of yourself.

674
00:35:17,560 --> 00:35:18,960
I am full of myself!

675
00:35:18,960 --> 00:35:19,800
So what?

676
00:35:19,800 --> 00:35:21,400
Sit down.

677
00:35:21,400 --> 00:35:22,400
Ignore her.

678
00:35:23,440 --> 00:35:24,240
Come on, let's drink.

679
00:35:31,680 --> 00:35:32,800
Let's come back and check it out later.

680
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:34,120
Yeah, let's go hang out over there first,

681
00:35:34,120 --> 00:35:35,240
and come back to buy it later.

682
00:35:35,240 --> 00:35:35,800
Okay.

683
00:35:35,800 --> 00:35:36,240
Bye-bye.

684
00:35:36,240 --> 00:35:36,920
Bye.

685
00:35:40,040 --> 00:35:41,560
Hi gorgeous, take a look.

686
00:35:46,200 --> 00:35:48,560
This is a bandana made with persimmon dye.

687
00:35:48,560 --> 00:35:49,720
Persimmon dye?

688
00:35:49,720 --> 00:35:50,680
Yes.

689
00:35:50,680 --> 00:35:53,520
I see this kind of blue tie-dye pretty often,

690
00:35:53,520 --> 00:35:54,520
but persimmon dye is...

691
00:35:54,520 --> 00:35:56,000
It's a type of plant dye.

692
00:35:56,000 --> 00:35:57,000
So what about the dye liquid?

693
00:35:57,000 --> 00:35:59,280
You use unripe little persimmons,

694
00:35:59,280 --> 00:36:00,880
mash them up and extract the juice.

695
00:36:00,880 --> 00:36:02,520
Then let it ferment for over a year.

696
00:36:03,040 --> 00:36:04,600
It takes over a year to ferment?

697
00:36:06,080 --> 00:36:06,920
In this persimmon dye,

698
00:36:06,920 --> 00:36:09,600
there are unique natural tannins and pectin.

699
00:36:09,600 --> 00:36:11,680
The dyed fabric holds up well to washing and sunlight.

700
00:36:11,680 --> 00:36:14,240
You can wash it and sun it often.

701
00:36:14,240 --> 00:36:14,840
This,

702
00:36:14,840 --> 00:36:17,000
is also an extension of the fabric's life.

703
00:36:17,560 --> 00:36:18,640
I can tell

704
00:36:18,640 --> 00:36:20,120
you really love tie-dyeing.

705
00:36:20,120 --> 00:36:20,840
Tie-dyeing

706
00:36:20,840 --> 00:36:22,680
is like when you randomly tie up a piece of cloth.

707
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:24,920
At first glance, it's a mess.

708
00:36:25,320 --> 00:36:27,120
But when you unfold it,

709
00:36:27,120 --> 00:36:28,680
every single piece is unique.

710
00:36:30,280 --> 00:36:31,160
That's true.

711
00:36:32,680 --> 00:36:33,840
I'll take one of these.

712
00:36:33,840 --> 00:36:36,320
And I'll take one of those persimmon dye bandanas too.

713
00:36:36,320 --> 00:36:36,760
Okay.

714
00:36:36,760 --> 00:36:37,440
Thank you.

715
00:36:51,840 --> 00:36:52,680
Sister Lan

716
00:36:52,680 --> 00:36:54,040
You know you can't hold your liquor.

717
00:36:54,040 --> 00:36:55,360
You should drink less.

718
00:36:59,040 --> 00:37:00,080
Here, drink this.

719
00:37:06,160 --> 00:37:07,320
If you ask me,

720
00:37:07,920 --> 00:37:09,560
Yiran is a good kid.

721
00:37:10,600 --> 00:37:12,840
She just has a sharp tongue, soft heart.

722
00:37:13,320 --> 00:37:14,320
True.

723
00:37:14,320 --> 00:37:17,400
I've watched Yiran grow up.

724
00:37:17,400 --> 00:37:20,000
She's a girl with such a good heart.

725
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:21,840
Alright, stop trying to comfort me.

726
00:37:23,400 --> 00:37:25,080
I'm a mother myself.

727
00:37:25,320 --> 00:37:28,040
How could I hold a grudge against my own daughter?

728
00:37:29,000 --> 00:37:30,400
For a woman,

729
00:37:30,640 --> 00:37:31,960
once she becomes a mother,

730
00:37:32,080 --> 00:37:33,400
she gains both armor

731
00:37:34,000 --> 00:37:35,160
and her Achilles' heel.

732
00:37:35,400 --> 00:37:36,960
Tell me about it.

733
00:37:46,440 --> 00:37:48,240
Looks like it's raining.

734
00:38:13,800 --> 00:38:14,600
Are you okay?

735
00:38:15,560 --> 00:38:16,360
I sprained my ankle.

736
00:38:17,280 --> 00:38:18,400
Let me carry you.

737
00:38:18,400 --> 00:38:19,160
Hold the umbrella.

738
00:38:31,520 --> 00:38:33,040
I thought you went back.

739
00:38:35,000 --> 00:38:36,640
The host family asked me to stay.

740
00:38:36,640 --> 00:38:37,960
There are still things to do tomorrow.

741
00:38:39,640 --> 00:38:40,760
Need any help?

742
00:38:41,800 --> 00:38:42,720
No need.

743
00:38:42,720 --> 00:38:43,640
It's so late.

744
00:38:45,440 --> 00:38:46,240
Besides,

745
00:38:46,880 --> 00:38:48,320
why aren't you in your room?

746
00:38:48,320 --> 00:38:49,360
What are you doing out here?

747
00:38:50,280 --> 00:38:51,240
Just wandering around.

748
00:38:55,320 --> 00:38:56,200
Look at this rain.

749
00:38:58,160 --> 00:38:59,120
What about it?

750
00:39:00,720 --> 00:39:03,160
It's part of the Earth's water cycle.

751
00:39:04,440 --> 00:39:06,640
Evaporating from the ground into the air,

752
00:39:06,640 --> 00:39:07,520
condensing into clouds,

753
00:39:07,520 --> 00:39:08,800
then falling back down,

754
00:39:08,800 --> 00:39:09,840
nourishing all living things.

755
00:39:10,560 --> 00:39:11,880
And then from the ground,

756
00:39:11,880 --> 00:39:14,320
evaporating into the air, condensing into clouds,

757
00:39:14,320 --> 00:39:15,320
and falling back down again,

758
00:39:15,320 --> 00:39:16,200
completing a cy...

759
00:39:16,600 --> 00:39:17,680
completing a cycle.

760
00:39:18,760 --> 00:39:19,520
Mr. Chen.

761
00:39:20,200 --> 00:39:21,680
Why the sudden science lesson?

762
00:39:23,560 --> 00:39:25,080
I just want to tell you

763
00:39:26,160 --> 00:39:27,280
that for many things,

764
00:39:27,280 --> 00:39:28,520
you don't necessarily have to pursue

765
00:39:28,520 --> 00:39:30,160
a result you're satisfied with.

766
00:39:30,160 --> 00:39:32,040
Instead, you should focus on the process.

767
00:39:32,040 --> 00:39:33,720
The process is very important.

768
00:39:34,280 --> 00:39:36,440
It can be endless

769
00:39:36,440 --> 00:39:37,760
and go on forever.

770
00:39:49,080 --> 00:39:50,160
Sister Lan.

771
00:39:50,160 --> 00:39:51,240
How's Yiran?

772
00:39:51,560 --> 00:39:52,240
She's fine.

773
00:39:52,440 --> 00:39:54,240
She sprained her ankle a bit,

774
00:39:54,560 --> 00:39:55,920
but I iced it for her.

775
00:39:56,160 --> 00:39:57,560
And I applied some safflower liniment.

776
00:39:58,480 --> 00:40:00,200
I don't think it'll swell up.

777
00:40:00,680 --> 00:40:01,320
Here.

778
00:40:04,120 --> 00:40:05,120
Sister Lan.

779
00:40:05,120 --> 00:40:07,400
Speaking from my experience as a mother,

780
00:40:07,960 --> 00:40:09,880
Yiran really cares about you.

781
00:40:10,080 --> 00:40:11,120
I know.

782
00:40:12,680 --> 00:40:14,360
She's just too stubborn to admit it.

783
00:40:14,360 --> 00:40:15,440
There's nothing I can do.

784
00:40:15,960 --> 00:40:16,880
We're mother and daughter.

785
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:18,640
I must owe her from my past life.

786
00:40:25,200 --> 00:40:26,120
Sister Lan.

787
00:40:27,760 --> 00:40:29,040
Thank you.

788
00:40:29,040 --> 00:40:29,960
For what?

789
00:40:29,960 --> 00:40:31,040
Don't be so polite.

790
00:40:32,240 --> 00:40:34,600
Having these few happy days,

791
00:40:35,120 --> 00:40:36,600
my life hasn't been in vain.

792
00:40:37,720 --> 00:40:38,320
Here.

793
00:40:39,960 --> 00:40:41,480
Why would I use that?

794
00:40:41,760 --> 00:40:42,760
Just put a little on.

795
00:40:43,080 --> 00:40:44,240
Let me tell you,

796
00:40:44,240 --> 00:40:46,160
you just came at the wrong time.

797
00:40:46,480 --> 00:40:48,200
If you had come a few months earlier,

798
00:40:48,880 --> 00:40:50,840
I could've taken you for mushroom hot pot.

799
00:40:50,840 --> 00:40:51,520
You have no idea,

800
00:40:51,520 --> 00:40:53,680
the mushrooms here are incredibly delicious.

801
00:40:53,720 --> 00:40:54,800
Have you heard of that?

802
00:40:54,800 --> 00:40:56,960
"Red cap, white stem,

803
00:40:56,960 --> 00:40:58,240
eat it and you'll shake,

804
00:40:58,240 --> 00:40:59,520
then lie on a wooden plank."

805
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:02,000
I haven't taken you to the zoo either.

806
00:41:02,600 --> 00:41:03,400
We could see alpacas.

807
00:41:03,400 --> 00:41:04,720
And we could also see those...

808
00:41:05,240 --> 00:41:05,720
those bears.

809
00:41:05,720 --> 00:41:06,960
I even played a bear before.

810
00:41:06,960 --> 00:41:07,640
Did you know?

811
00:41:07,640 --> 00:41:08,400
Really.

812
00:41:08,400 --> 00:41:10,280
You think I'm kidding you, don't you?

813
00:41:10,280 --> 00:41:11,160
Next time you come,

814
00:41:11,880 --> 00:41:13,760
bring your older son along.

815
00:41:14,080 --> 00:41:17,560
Young people nowadays love escape rooms.

816
00:41:19,040 --> 00:41:20,200
I've dressed up as a ghost,

817
00:41:20,200 --> 00:41:21,520
and as a fox spirit.

818
00:41:21,520 --> 00:41:22,960
I even played Maggie Cheung once.

819
00:41:23,560 --> 00:41:25,840
When I was a ghost, I wasn't scary at all.

820
00:41:25,840 --> 00:41:27,160
Later, I covered my face in blood.

821
00:41:27,160 --> 00:41:29,040
I scared them so much they screamed and ran.

822
00:41:29,040 --> 00:41:30,400
And I'd go catch them.

823
00:41:30,560 --> 00:41:31,560
Next time you come over,

824
00:41:31,560 --> 00:41:33,400
I'll personally be an NPC for you guys.

825
00:41:33,400 --> 00:41:34,640
Do you know what an NPC is?

826
00:41:35,200 --> 00:41:37,640
It's someone who scares people in escape rooms.

827
00:41:39,840 --> 00:41:40,440
Right.

828
00:41:40,880 --> 00:41:42,080
That rascal Zhang Lijuan,

829
00:41:42,360 --> 00:41:44,200
she even said next time,

830
00:41:44,200 --> 00:41:46,320
we should each get a cheongsam made.

831
00:41:46,960 --> 00:41:47,960
I was thinking,

832
00:41:47,960 --> 00:41:49,600
Wang Daren could get a Mao suit.

833
00:41:49,600 --> 00:41:52,240
Us three in cheongsams playing mahjong,

834
00:41:52,240 --> 00:41:53,520
it'd feel like Wang Daren

835
00:41:53,520 --> 00:41:55,160
had married three concubines.

836
00:41:55,720 --> 00:41:57,880
That old bachelor would be thrilled.

837
00:41:58,840 --> 00:42:00,120
Let me pick a cheongsam.

838
00:42:00,640 --> 00:42:01,960
This one looks okay.

839
00:42:01,960 --> 00:42:03,000
Look.

840
00:42:04,880 --> 00:42:05,880
Hong Yu.

841
00:42:09,440 --> 00:42:11,280
You fell asleep so fast.

842
00:42:11,280 --> 00:42:12,840
Out like a light.

843
00:42:15,680 --> 00:42:16,960
You must be a bit tired.

844
00:42:18,320 --> 00:42:19,040
Just sleep.

845
00:42:19,040 --> 00:42:20,400
You're exhausted.

846
00:42:58,640 --> 00:42:59,560
Yiran.

847
00:43:00,280 --> 00:43:01,320
Let me help you.

848
00:43:01,680 --> 00:43:02,520
It's fine, Auntie Juan.

849
00:43:02,520 --> 00:43:03,360
I can do it myself.

850
00:43:04,280 --> 00:43:05,280
Have some water then.

851
00:43:09,360 --> 00:43:11,920
Your mom always said your stubborn temper was like hers.

852
00:43:12,160 --> 00:43:13,360
I think so too.

853
00:43:14,520 --> 00:43:16,000
She's got some nerve saying that.

854
00:43:18,640 --> 00:43:19,800
